                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Pros\n+ Amazing Graphics\n+ Smooth Animations\n+ Challenging levels with optional collectibles that allow completionist and explorer players to have some more fun\n+ A game that doesn't waste your time. You'll probably die a lot, but respawning is very quick. \n+ A hella lot of great platforming content for the price!\n+ Strong Rayman Legends vibe, specially on the enemies\n\nCons\n- Pretty nasty hitboxes. Sometimes enemy hits really don't feel like they should hit. In my opinion, enemy hitboxes should be smaller to give players a higher chance of survival\n- I'm sure I've watched a pretty awesome animated movie showing this game's story on YouTube. Why isn't it in the game??\n- Instead of just \"continue, restart and exit\", it should have a \"Next Level\" option on the level's completion menu. This would allow players to advance even more quickly\n- Gamepad controls should be a little reworked. Moving the analog right makes you go right, that's fine, but moving the analog DOWN makes you go right, which should'nt happen.\n\nDefinitely worth the price!",
